AB  - The Polymath Virtual Library is the main project of the Ignacio Larramendi Foundation. Its objective is to make accessible the thinking of Spanish, Portuguese, Brazilian and Latin American authors of all time. It aggregates and groups the works of these authors in digital format. The Virtual Polygraph Library has been a case study for the W3C Library Linked Data Incubator Group (Cluster: Bibliographic Data) and the Europeana Data Model. Authority records and bibliographic resources are catalogued following RDA. The Polymath Virtual Library uses Linked Open Data (LOD) technology, specifically the Europeana Data Model (EDM). Among the main Linked Open Data resources it uses are Wikidata, VIAF, DBpedia, Library of Congress Linked Service, Gemeinsame Normdatei, data.bnf.fr, datos.bne.es and WorldCat Identities.
